the athletes luxury home is a shell now  cleared of all his belongings including  his medals and running trophies a silent  empty reminder of the event which  changed his life forever  and violently cut short his model  girlfriends the athletes bedroom seems a  lot smaller somehow without all his  possessions and this is the corridor he  headed down gun in hand towards the  bathroom  it was here he told police he heard  noises coming from behind the toilet  door noises he insists he believed were  made by an intruder the four bullets the  runner fired through the locked toilet  door ended the life of reeva Steenkamp  who was behind it just what the athlete  was thinking when he picked up his  9-millimeter pistol formed the backbone  of the long-running trial police  photographs taken hours after the  shooting showed the runner drenched in  his girlfriend's blood which version  will the judge decide on will she  believe the prosecution's version that  the athlete chased his girlfriend down  this corridor and into the bathroom  where she barricaded herself in the  toilet and he deliberately fired four  shots intending to kill her or will she  believe the athletes version that he was  so unstable on his stomps he had to lean  here and after fear for his life  and his girlfriends he fired towards the  toilet cubicle believing that his life  and his girlfriends was at risk the  athlete was in the witness box for seven  days insisting he never intended to kill  his girlfriend Lauren stood up to the  door sort of hitting that side and I  think I had it three times from the door  open I threw it open and I set over Eva  and I cried  along  mr. Pistorius but the prosecution solved  differently I made a mistake  you killed leave us can't come that's  what you did I made a mistake you see  you're repeating it three times what was  your mistake  you killed her you shot and killed it  work you take responsibility for that  my lady that's how you think say yes I  killed I shot and killed three versed in  God took my lady  okay the toilet cubicle still bears the  scars of the shooting the yellow  stickers were placed there by the police  the athletes house has now been sold  everything packed up and moved out the  Pistorius family say he could never face  living in the house again but he also  had to raise funds to pay for his very  expensive legal costs but this house  will be forever remembered for what  happened in the early hours of  Valentine's Day 2013  Alex Crawford Sky News Pretoria
 

